      "body": "## Background\n\n`repr(LLM(...))` calls `collective_rpc(\"get_model_inspection\")`. The default `WorkerBase.get_model_inspection()` passes `self.get_model()` to `format_model_inspection`, which assumes a torch `nn.Module` and walks `named_children()`.\n\n## Problem\n\nOut-of-tree platforms can serve non-torch models — for example vllm-metal serves MLX models. Calling `repr(LLM(...))` in a debugger or inspector raises:\n\n```\nAttributeError: 'Model' object has no attribute 'named_children'\n```\n\nThe vllm-metal plugin worked around this by overriding `get_model_inspection()` in its worker, but every other out-of-tree platform hits the same wall. Root issue: the default `WorkerBase` doesn't handle non-torch models.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd an `isinstance(model, nn.Module)` guard in `WorkerBase.get_model_inspection()`. Non-torch models fall back to `repr(model)` instead of crashing in `format_model_inspection`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m py_compile vllm/v1/worker/worker_base.py` — syntax OK\n- Fix is pure defensive with zero behavior change for the torch path\n- Out-of-tree platforms no longer need to override `get_model_inspection()` just for repr() to work\n\n## AI Disclosure\n\nAI assistance was used to identify the root cause, draft the fix, and write the PR description. I reviewed and tested the change myself.\n\nRefs #61366",
